  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">Servus proprius quando haeres institu-</l>
    <l n="3">tus fiat liber?</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Servus alienus licet dominus sit defun-</l>
    <l n="6">ctus vel in utero, hae-</l>
    <l n="7">res institui poterit.</l>
    <l n="8" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">Servus plurium haeres institui poterit.</l>
    <l n="10" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="11">1. Plures in infinitum haeredes institui po-</l>
    <l n="12">terunt.</l>
    <l n="13">2. Moribus quid obtineat?</l>
    <l n="14">3. Quid jure Canonico?</l>
    <l n="15" para="true">§. 5. 6. 7. 8.</l>
    <l n="16">1. Hareditas in 12. partes dividitur, &amp;</l>
    <l n="17">cur ita?</l>
    <l n="18">2. Ex re certa nemo scribi potest haeres.</l>
    <l n="19">3. Varii casus circa portiones assignantur.</l>
    <l n="20">4. Mores enarrantur.</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">§. 9.</l>
    <l n="22">1. Modi instituendi varii, quorum alii</l>
    <l n="23">illiciti, alii liciti.</l>
    <l n="24">2. Quid moribus?</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">§. 10.</l>
    <l n="26">1. Quotuplex sit conditio, &amp; quis effect-</l>
    <l n="27">us?</l>
    <l n="28" para="true">§. 11.</l>
    <l n="29">1. Effectus conditionum plurium descri-</l>
    <l n="30">buntur.</l>
    <l n="31">2. Quid moribus?</l>
    <l n="32" para="true">§. 12.</l>
    <l n="33" para="true">Peregre nati, &amp; peregrinantes haeredes</l>
    <l n="34">institui poterunt.</l>
    <l n="35" type="heading" level="1" caput="2" para="true">LIBR. 2. TIT. 15.</l>
    <l n="36" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De vulgari substitutione.</l>
    <l n="37" para="true">1. Substitutio definitur.</l>
    <l n="38" para="true">2. Omnis substitutio in casum est facta.</l>
    <l n="39" type="heading" level="1" para="true">E X</l>
    <l n="40" para="true">3. Tres sunt modi vulgaris substitutionis.</l>
    <l n="41" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="42" para="true">Quid sit breviloqua &amp; reciproca substi-</l>
    <l n="43">tutio?</l>
    <l n="44" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="45" para="true">Partes in institutione posita, censentur</l>
    <l n="46">repetita in substitutione.</l>
    <l n="47" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="48" para="true">Secundo substitutus etiam primo substi-</l>
    <l n="49">tutus est.</l>
    <l n="50" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="51" para="true">1. Casus excepti, quibus cum instituto sub-</l>
    <l n="52">stitutus admittitur.</l>
    <l n="53" para="true">2. Sensus formula vulgaris substitutionis</l>
    <l n="54">explicatur.</l>
    <l n="55" para="true">3. Mores enarrantur.</l>
    <l n="56" type="heading" level="1" para="true">LIBR. 2. INSTIT. TIT. 16.</l>
    <l n="57" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Pupill. substit.</l>
    <l n="58" para="true">1. VNI dua substitutionum species.</l>
    <l n="59" para="true">2. Pupillaris à vulgari multis modis</l>
    <l n="60">distinguitur.</l>
    <l n="61" para="true">3. Quis substituat pupillariter, &amp; qui-</l>
    <l n="62">bus?</l>
    <l n="63" para="true">4. Origo pupillaris substitutionis discribi-</l>
    <l n="64">tur.</l>
    <l n="65" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="66" para="true">1. Quid sit quasi pupillaris substitutio?</l>
    <l n="67" para="true">2. Quot modis à pupillari distinguatur?</l>
    <l n="68" para="true">3. Quot modis finiatur?</l>
    <l n="69" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="70" para="true">Unum est testamentum in substitutione</l>
    <l n="71">pupillari, &amp; quodammodo duplex.</l>
    <l n="72" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="73" para="true">Cautela in pupillari substitutione ob-</l>
    <l n="74">servanda.</l>
    <l n="75" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="76" para="true">Exheredato pupillariter substituì potest.</l>
    <l n="77" para="true">§. 5.</l>
